{
  "layout": "stack",
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "status",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "value": "## Git &amp; GitHub CLI"
        },
        {
          "type": "auth_status",
          "bind": "GET /api/apps/git/status",
          "logout_action": {
            "call": "POST /api/apps/git/logout"
          },
          "loading_text": "Checking GitHub login…",
          "logged_in_text": "Logged in as {username}",
          "logged_out_text": "Not signed in."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "credential",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "auth_status",
          "bind": "GET /api/apps/git/status",
          "loading_text": "",
          "logged_in_text": "Token {token_masked}  ·  {token_kind}\n\nScopes: {scopes_text}",
          "logged_out_text": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "collapsible",
          "title": "Update token",
          "collapsed": true,
          "widgets": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "value": "Paste a **personal access token** to replace the stored credential. Saving signs `gh` in immediately and re-mirrors it to every agent container.\n\nThe device-flow button only ever grants what aw-app-git's OAuth App requests (`repo`, `read:org`, `gist`, `workflow`) — it **cannot** grant `write:packages` or `admin:org`. Publishing an app image to GHCR or managing an org runner group needs a PAT with those scopes."
            },
            {
              "type": "form",
              "id": "token_update",
              "submit": {
                "call": "POST /api/apps/git/settings"
              },
              "submit_label": "Save token",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "github_token",
                  "label": "GitHub personal access token",
                  "input": "password",
                  "placeholder": "ghp_… / github_pat_…",
                  "description": "Stored in the zero-knowledge secret store, never in plain config. Re-applied on every boot."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "device-login",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "value": "### Sign in with GitHub\nClick to get a one-time code, then open [github.com/login/device](https://github.com/login/device) and enter it there — login is detected automatically, no need to click anything else."
        },
        {
          "type": "button",
          "hide_when_logged_in": true,
          "label": "Sign in with GitHub",
          "action": {
            "call": "POST /api/apps/git/device/start",
            "poll": {
              "call": "POST /api/apps/git/device/poll",
              "interval_ms": 3000,
              "timeout_ms": 900000,
              "done_field": "status",
              "done_values": [
                "success",
                "expired_token",
                "access_denied",
                "error"
              ],
              "pending_text": "Waiting for authorization on [github.com/login/device](https://github.com/login/device)…",
              "timeout_text": "Timed out waiting for authorization — click Sign in with GitHub again."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "advanced",
      "widgets": [
        {
          "type": "collapsible",
          "title": "Advanced / git identity",
          "collapsed": true,
          "widgets": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "value": "Git commit identity and, rarely, your own OAuth App for the Sign in with GitHub button."
            },
            {
              "type": "form",
              "id": "advanced_settings",
              "submit": {
                "call": "POST /api/apps/git/settings"
              },
              "submit_label": "Save",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "key": "git_user_name",
                  "label": "Git user.name",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "Jane Doe"
                },
                {
                  "key": "git_user_email",
                  "label": "Git user.email",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "jane@example.com"
                },
                {
                  "key": "oauth_client_id",
                  "label": "OAuth App client_id (custom)",
                  "input": "text",
                  "placeholder": "Ov23liWR67ZgY2P6fYKh (default, already configured)",
                  "description": "Only set this if you want to use your own GitHub OAuth App for the Sign in with GitHub button instead of aw-app-git's public one."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
